CODEGEN.md §2.4, §2.9 (DECISIONS 341): a load of a text file an earlier build wrote is refused at the load; a load of a hand-written file of the same output directory is not.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Note.
@text("note.txt")
export fn note() -> String { return "n\n" }

/// Kept.
let kept: String = load.text("gen/hand.txt")

/// Fed.
let fed: String = load.text("gen/note.txt")

emit text { out: "gen" }
-- a/gen/hand.txt --
hand
-- a/gen/note.txt --
n
-- findings.txt --
error[E8026]  a/a.canon:12:19
  a/gen/note.txt is read by this load and written by emit text of a: an output is never an input of its own build

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
